{"entries":[{"entry_key":"CLM_1","claim_class":"unknown","claim":"The bounded catalog contains no source, evidence, event, trace, formal observation, or formal artifact handles sufficient to identify the safest reclamation protocol for a deterministic per-problem workspace after a crash without terminal record, nor to specify what that protocol must durably record.","scratch_handles":["SCR_1","SCR_2","SCR_3"]}],"uncovered_requirements":[{"requirement":"Formal artifact handles, evidence handles, or source handles defining deterministic workspace reclamation protocols and the durable records required to prevent silent displacement of completed evidence.","reason":"The bounded catalog is limited to scratch handles (SCR_1, SCR_2, SCR_3) and a process observation (PRC_1) that does not substantiate any protocol.","related_entry_keys":["CLM_1"],"scratch_handles":["SCR_1","SCR_2","SCR_3"]},{"requirement":"Evidence or trace handles establishing whether the deterministic workspace interacts with wall-clock time, physical randomness, or non-reproducible oracle inputs, and whether completed evidence is content-addressed or path-addressed.","reason":"Scratch excerpts SCR_1, SCR_2, and SCR_3 advance incompatible models (hidden non-determinism, Merkle-DAG immutability, pure determinism) without grounding handles to adjudicate among them.","related_entry_keys":["CLM_1"],"scratch_handles":["SCR_1","SCR_2","SCR_3"]}]}